@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Privacy policy and data handling information for the ContainSharp website.";
    ViewData["CanonicalUrl"] = "https://containsharp.com/Privacy";
}

<div class="briefing-stage">
    <partial name="_PageHeaderPartial" view-data='@(new ViewDataDictionary(ViewData) {
        { "Icon", "shield-lock" },
        { "HeaderTitle", "Privacy Policy" },
        { "HeaderDescription", "What ContainSharp stores, why, and how to opt out." },
        { "HeaderTokenColor", "comment" }
    })' />

    <article class="content-card" data-token="comment">
        <div class="page-prose">
            <h2>What we collect</h2>
            <p>
                ContainSharp is a personal technology-watch dashboard. The site itself does not require an account.
                The only personal data we deliberately store is the email address you provide when subscribing to the
                daily newsletter.
            </p>

            <h2>Newsletter subscribers</h2>
            <p>
                When you subscribe, we store your email address, the subscription date, and a confirmation token used
                only to validate that the address belongs to you. We do not enrich, sell, or share this information
                with any third party.
            </p>
            <p>
                You can request unsubscription at any time from the
                <a asp-page="/Newsletter">Unsubscribe</a> page. The process uses a confirmation email so nobody else
                can unsubscribe you without your consent. Once confirmed, your email address is removed from our
                active list.
            </p>

            <h2>Analytics and logs</h2>
            <p>
                Standard web server logs are kept for short-term operational purposes (debugging, abuse prevention).
                They typically include the requested URL, response status, user agent, and a truncated IP. No
                third-party analytics or advertising scripts run on the site.
            </p>

            <h2>Hosting and data location</h2>
            <p>
                The site and database are hosted on standard cloud infrastructure inside the European Union.
                Communication is encrypted in transit via HTTPS.
            </p>

            <h2>Your rights</h2>
            <p>
                Under the GDPR, you have the right to access, correct, or erase the personal data we hold about you,
                and to object to its processing. For any of these requests, write to the contact listed on the
                <a asp-page="/About">About</a> page.
            </p>

            <h2>Updates</h2>
            <p>
                This policy may evolve as the site changes. Material updates will be noted on this page; significant
                changes affecting newsletter subscribers will be announced inside the newsletter itself.
            </p>
        </div>
    </article>
</div>
